module gunbc.roadmap_site_surface_types

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr }
import std.content_hash { Fnv1a64Structural }
import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }

// A HEALTHZ READ IS A COPRODUCT AND ALWAYS WAS -- this declaration now says so.
//
// It used to be a two-field record whose discriminant was carried as "which field did I leave
// empty". Every one of its twenty constructions set exactly one field; not one ever set both,
// because there is no such observation: a probe either landed and produced a body, or it refused
// and produced a reason. The empty string was doing the work of a tag, in a type that also admits
// the empty string as a legitimate body.
//
// WHAT THE COPRODUCT REMOVES, and both are state-space reductions rather than added checks.
// A refusal no longer HAS a body field, so reading a body off a failed probe is unwritable rather
// than merely wrong -- and the consumer that used to guarantee this by checking probe_error first
// now cannot get it wrong in any order, because the compiler will not let it reach a body it does
// not have. And { body: "x", probe_error: "y" } -- representable before, meaningless always -- has
// no legitimate constructor: nothing can produce it through either variant. It can still be SPELLED
// as a bare record literal, which is the one place this climb stops short; the rung block below
// measures exactly where, rather than letting this paragraph round it up.
//
// THE RUNG, MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS RATHER THAN ASSERTED -- and it is TWO rungs, because the
// two ways of writing the invalid state are refused at two different times.
//
// FIELD ACCESS IS STRUCTURAL. `read.body` against this carrier is a located resolve-time refusal:
// `error: no field 'body' on type 'HealthzEffectiveRead'`, reported during strict-preparation with
// modules_resolved=3729, before a single witness executes. A probe was written to reach a body off
// a HealthzProbeRefused and the floor refused to prepare at all. So the headline claim -- a refusal
// has no body to read -- is structurally guaranteed, and it is in fact broader than that: the
// carrier has no fields at the type level, so every field-access route into it is gone, not just
// the one on the refusal arm.
//
// THE BARE RECORD LITERAL IS NOT. Writing `HealthzEffectiveRead { body: .., probe_error: .. }` --
// the old shape, tagging no variant -- still RESOLVES and still constructs; it is refused only when
// something matches on it, at evaluation, as `non-exhaustive pattern match on: HealthzEffectiveRead
// { body: .., probe_error: .. }`. Measured, not inferred: the pre-change probe passed on the record
// and the same source became a per-witness runtime FAIL after the coproduct landed, with the corpus
// fully executed (planned=9784) rather than refused in preparation.
//
// So the honest ceiling for the CONSTRUCTION half is mechanically preventable, not structurally
// impossible: the invalid value is writable, and what stops it is a runtime refusal that has to
// execute. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, and it is a compiler capability rather than anything this module can
// author: a record literal naming a coproduct type with no variant tag should refuse at resolve,
// where the field-access form already does. Until that lands, saying this carrier makes the state
// unwritable would be the rung inflation DESIGN §4b calls worse than sitting low -- which is why
// the paragraph above says what it says, and why the probes that established it are cited here by
// their measurement rather than left enrolled: both are hard refusals, so neither can survive in
// the corpus as an executing control.
//
// WHAT IT DOES NOT REMOVE, stated so this row is not read as more than it is. Readiness grounds in
// five ordered stages (probe, parse, identity, revision, surface) and this makes only the FIRST
// structural. The other four remain ordering-by-discipline inside
// gunbc.live_deploy.readiness ground_service_ready_from_healthz_with_bundle; see that module's
// readiness_check_order_note, which now names the four that remain rather than all five.
type HealthzEffectiveRead
  = HealthzBodyRead { body: String }
  | HealthzProbeRefused { probe_error: String }

type RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact {
  url_path: NonEmptyStr
  body: String
  digest: Fnv1a64Structural
}

type RoadmapSiteSurfaceBundle {
  subject_identity: Fnv1a64Structural
  producer_identity: Fnv1a64Structural
  bundle_identity: Fnv1a64Structural
  roadmap_md: RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact
  dispatch_json: RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact
  daily_html: RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact
  full_html: RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact
  dispatch_js: RoadmapSiteSurfaceArtifact
  healthz_body: String
}

type LiveRoadmapSiteSurfaceBundle {
  subject: String
  bundle: RoadmapSiteSurfaceBundle
}

data roadmap_site_surface_subject: String = "gunbc.roadmap_static_site/live-tree"

data roadmap_site_surface_bundle_schema_note: String = "ONE semantic snapshot per operation: authority projected once, surface rendered once, healthz serialized once. subject_identity hashes acceptance plus roadmap/dispatch document bodies (or the exact typed refusal detail). producer_identity names the observe/render implementation. bundle_identity joins the five served-artifact digests. RoadmapSiteSurfaceBundle is the retained carrier every readiness witness and production healthz path evaluates — member predicates take the bundle as an argument and cannot re-invoke filesystem, Git, authority projection, or rendering producers."
